cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the associated article once published."
type: software
title: "herv-rna-regulation: analysis workflow for HERV-derived RNA regulatory potential in the human transcriptome"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/funcgen/herv-rna-regulation"
abstract: >-
  Validated analysis workflow (Python, R and Bash) that characterises the RNA regulatory potential of 53,176 human
  endogenous retrovirus (HERV) internal regions and 560,594 HERV long terminal repeats in GRCh38 (GENCODE release 48):
  composition-controlled RNA-binding protein motif enrichment, HERV overlap with transcript features, conserved
  retroviral domains in terminal exons, HERV contribution to lncRNA genes, lncRNA functional annotation, and
  SPARCS-like antisense LTR configurations at transcript termini.
keywords:
  - human endogenous retroviruses
  - HERV
  - long terminal repeats
  - RNA-binding proteins
  - long non-coding RNA
  - transcript architecture
  - SPARCS
  - transposable elements
  - bioinformatics workflow
